WEBVTT

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.570
...Takasu-san had agreed to produce the same song for Wakamatsu Madoka.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.620
Then... who should we ask to be Full Moon's Producer?

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.070
Well, then...

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.870
...I wonder what's going to happen today.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:23.450
Huh?

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.820
Do you understand?

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.670
Yes.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.380
Paging Dr. Nakamura.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.550
Please contact the front desk immediately.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.550
Paging Dr. Nakamura.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.890
Please contact the front desk immediately...

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.890
Come on.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.020
O-Okay...

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.270
What's wrong?

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.230
Aren't you going to knock?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:19.820
Huh?

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:20.900
What's up, Mitsuki-chan?

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:21.730
Why are you here?

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:24.440
Ah.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.820
Um... that's...

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.910
I just happened to be in the area...

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.840
B-Bye.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.210
I see...

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.920
It's not an easy thing to ask for, huh...

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.170
I'll talk to him myself then.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.720
Mitsuki, you just wait there.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.470
Okay...

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.630
Sorry...

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:54.270
Hey, I'm the one who should be sighing.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.350
Why didn't you just ask him?

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:57.560
That's 'cause...

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.400
What am I supposed to say...?

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.980
It's like a little kid playing make-believe...

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.320
I feel like I'm dragging Wakaouji-sensei into this...

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.530
We're not playing make-believe here!

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:09.160
Man, you worry way too much!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.320
Anyways, you know...

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.530
It's not acting child-like.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.740
Y-You think?

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.500
It's not child-like, is it...?

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.750
And what's with that Takuto...

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.880
He's the one who said that we should all go 
together, and then he's like...

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.540
"It be better if I didn't".

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.880
What's he trying to do?!

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:24.760
Ah...

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.590
When Takuto said that he shouldn't, he wasn't lying.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:28.630
What do you mean?

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.760
Wakaouji-sensei, that is...

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.600
I guess he doesn't really like him...

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.810
Why's that?

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:12.510
So... if we have a former member of Route L as the producer,

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:18.850
then we can use that to target old fans of Route L and draw them in as well.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.560
It'd be something like this.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:23.770
Wow...

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:26.030
It's like grown-ups doing business...

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.490
I refuse.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:32.200
Eh?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.410
C-Can you tell me why?

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:37.160
Ah...

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.660
I'll tell you the truth.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:43.380
If you don't produce it, then this plan won't be possible.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.340
For Mitsuki's sake...

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.340
...can you please do this?

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:50.010
I refuse.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.510
Why?!

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:52.840
My reason doesn't matter.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.510
No way...

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.390
You're the only one I can ask Dr. Wakaouji!

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.140
They're really going at it now...

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.480
You should understand how hard it is!

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.070
This will be the conceptual image that we're going to use.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:54.070
Q-Quite untraditional...

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.530
But, it seems like a mismatch...

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.450
You hit it right on the nose.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:05:59.620
Is is a mismatch.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:00.430
Eh?

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.250
On top of the appeal that her raw, primitive feel has,

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.580
I'll throw in something completely different to complement it.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:08.380
Understand?

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:09.920
Y-Yeah...

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:14.720
Which means that I want each of you to keep this conceptual image in mind.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:15.880
Any questions?

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.810
<i>Hey! Look here please!</i>

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.360
<i>Madoka-chan, over here!</i>

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.980
<i>Okay!</i>

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:44.960
Sorry...

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.120
I guess the plan was flawed.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.830
We'll have to patch things up.

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:51.630
But... how do we do that...

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.340
Um...

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:55.550
Ooshige-san...

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:57.180
It might be a problem for him.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.340
Hey. Don't say that.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.010
It's your song.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:01.970
Yeah...

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.890
Hey... Mitsuki...

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.520
Why do you have a pillow?

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.850
Wh... what?

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:09.900
What?!

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.620
What?

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:26.580
Oh, boy...

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.790
Meroko's also...

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:33.340
...begging you too! {}

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.000
...begging you too! {}

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:34.670
...begging you too! {}

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:35.710
...begging you too! {}

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:45.770
Can you give that back?

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.270
If I give it back, will you listen to our request?

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.110
Now, look here...

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:55.610
Pretty please!

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:05.330
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:05.740
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:06.200
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:06.750
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:07.200
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:07.700
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:08.370
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.620
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.420
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:11.920
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:12.460
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:13.000
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.090
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.360
Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please! Please!

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:17.920
You're bothering me.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.720
Man!

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.720
What's with that doctor?!

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:25.220
He's got that attitude despite knowing that she doesn't have much time yet.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.810
He said last time... that he couldn't accept the fact...

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:28.600
Yeah...

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.190
Basically, about her lifespan...

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.730
It's not like I don't understand his views as a doctor,

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:35.770
but he's way too hard-headed!

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:36.650
Huh?

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:38.740
Hey, hey.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.950
What have you been doing?

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:42.450
Oh, just a little...

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.160
Let's see...

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.460
What?

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.630
What is she doing?

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.130
Amidakuji, I guess...

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.390
Again?

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.190
Ah!

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.650
What are you doing?

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.480
It'll be the same no matter how many times you keep doing it.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:19.110
No matter which one comes up, 
you'll never be satisfied, will you?

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:22.940
Besides, what are you thinking, using amidakuji to decide this...

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.450
You're right...

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:28.200
That doctor...

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.700
I'm sure he could tell...

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.160
...that you aren't sure about how you feel yet.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.920
I get it.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.880
So that's why he said no, huh?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.460
Be clear about your own feelings first.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.420
I agree!

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.970
You know, I...

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.680
...I could never give up on music...

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:51.140
But Wakaouji-sensei gave it up for good...

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.810
...even though he loved music.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:58.360
It must have been a hard thing to do.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:00.570
Much harder than what I'm going through...

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:02.490
Maybe.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.280
But, just because of that...

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.950
...you're not going to say that you're giving up <i>Eternal Snow</i>, right?

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:09.240
Well...

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.490
I won't give up on it.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.410
Is that so...

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:14.710
Then... everything's okay.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.630
What do we have to do next?

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:24.670
We're studying the movement of the constellations and the Moon.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.090
Eh?!

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:30.140
You got your own computer?!

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:31.060
Yep!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.390
Must be nice...

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:34.270
My daddy's so kind.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:37.150
He'll do anything I ask!

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:40.570
Kind? More like he's spoiling you...

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.110
You're so mean!

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.700
<i>Wakaouji-sensei!</i>

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.990
<i>I have a favor to ask!</i> {}

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:51.790
<i>Please be my producer!</i>

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.910
<i>If Mitsuki-chan's asking me, 
I can't very well refuse.</i>

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:55.830
<i>Yay!</i>

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:57.330
<i>I'm so happy!</i>

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:00.090
<i>I love you, Wakaouji-sensei!</i>

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:04.510
That kind of conversation could never happen...

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.390
We want to do <i>Eternal Snow</i>... no matter what!

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.600
Why are you so determined on doing that?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.850
Because... you're telling us to change the song, boss!

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:15.180
In reality, that won't work.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.480
You can't do <i>Eternal Snow.</i>

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.060
You haven't even found anyone who's willing to produce it.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.320
I'm currently talking it over with someone.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:25.650
And you think that Seed Records will be okay with that person...?

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.900
I believe that they will be!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.410
I didn't want to say this, but...

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.410
...if you keep this up, I'll have to transfer you.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.200
Transfer?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.620
You mean... change managers?

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.080
To put it bluntly, that's correct.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.960
T-That's...

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.480
This is Cassiopeia at seven o'clock.

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:09.990
Here... two hours later, at nine o'clock...

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:14.370
It shape has stayed the same,
but its position has changed like so.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:16.160
Yes.

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:17.040
Excellent job.'

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.040
Return to your seat.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:22.420
What's wrong?

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.540
You don't look to happy.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.420
It's nothing, I'm fine.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:34.260
As Maijima explained...

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:37.310
...the shape of the constellation does not change as time passes...

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.520
However, the position in the sky <i>do </i> change.

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.230
Then, next...

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:44.810
...let's look at the relationship between the Earth and the Moon.

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:47.820
The Moon as everyone knows...

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.780
...doesn't shine by itself.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:50.490
Eh?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.740
Do you know what makes it shine, then?

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.450
Hasegawa, do you know?

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:01.720
I'll go try and ask him!

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:07.190
M-Mitsuki?

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:10.690
Can the teacher ask for something too?

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.900
Please, I'd like you to sit down.

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.620
Kouyama-san did it again!

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.170
So, what did you need?

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:29.000
Wakaouji-sensei, I'm begging you.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.630
Please accept the position as my producer!

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.130
So that's what this is about.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.970
You know, even if it's Mitsuki-chan who's asking me...

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:40.350
...there's some things that I can do, and some things that I just can't.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:45.060
I understand what you mean, but I still have to ask you...

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:46.940
Wakaouji-sensei...

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.560
...I want you to help me do <i>Eternal Snow</i> !

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:52.530
That's impossible, Mitsuki-chan.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.780
I'm happy you feel that way, though...

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:57.200
I see...

00:14:58.070 --> 00:14:59.450
Doesn't he have any regrets?

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:00.240
Eh?

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.410
What did you just say?

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:04.080
I said, doesn't he have any regrets?

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.750
W-What do you mean?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.330
Mitsuki-chan, who are you...

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.290
Could it be those two...

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:14.880
She won't ask you, so I'm going to do it myself.

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:15.920
You.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:18.150
So you really don't feel anything for music now?

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:20.600
Nothing at all.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.810
I'm so envious...

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:24.600
What do you mean?

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.640
Well, I'm a Shinigami...

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:30.060
I see all kinds of people in my line of work

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.320
Every one of them... dies with regrets...

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.980
If only I had done that...

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:37.260
If only I had done this...

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:39.320
S-Stop it Takuto!

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:40.870
This isn't something I should be saying, but...

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.910
...while you're still alive is the only time when you can do what you love. {edited}

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.370
That means that you have to give it your all!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:51.080
I don't want to hear that from a Shinigami.

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:53.210
I suppose so.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:56.260
On top of that, I look like a stuffed animal.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.550
I'm probably not convincing at all.

00:15:58.550 --> 00:15:59.760
But, you know...

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:01.550
...it's just like I said.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:04.010
You can only do what you love while you're alive.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:06.600
That's why she's working so hard.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:08.520
While what little is left of her life...

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.560
With that tiny body of hers...

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:13.900
There will be suffering... there will be sadness...

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:16.330
But, if she can sing a song that she loves...

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.950
I-I'm sorry, Wakaouji-sensei!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.990
Sorry to be a bother to you. {edited}

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:24.160
Excuse us!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.420
Hey, you damn brat!

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:43.240
Only while you're still alive, huh...

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:45.660
Geez!

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:47.660
Geez! Stupid Takuto!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:51.200
Why'd you say all those things to Wakaouji-sensei!

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.580
Hey! I couldn't just stand there any longer!

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.460
Hey, hey...

00:17:58.460 --> 00:17:59.670
Did something happen?

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:00.670
The hell if I know!

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:01.760
That blockhead...

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:02.630
Oh...

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:05.360
So you're going to let me be the odd one out?

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.090
Fine!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:14.480
Late...

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:15.310
Yeah...

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:16.850
I wonder what's wrong.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:18.750
Mitsuki...

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:20.690
Ooshige-san!

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.320
Sorry... I'm late...

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:27.280
What's wrong? You look awful...

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.530
I drank too much last night.

00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:30.540
Broken heart?

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.330
No, I was just pissed off...

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:33.160
About what?

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.790
My boss...

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:38.130
Wait, that doesn't have anything to do with you!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.130
Come on, let's go to work.

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:43.590
Ooshige-san...

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:45.340
That's dangerous...

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:57.230
Okay, good job!

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:58.850
Thank you very much.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:00.610
Good work.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.900
Is your headache any better?

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:07.200
A little, I guess...

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:10.620
Wa-Wakaouji-sensei!

00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:15.120
The offer that you made a few days ago...

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:17.330
I spent some time thinking over it carefully.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:19.500
Sensei, I'm very sorry about that!

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.590
We won't bother you...

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:24.550
...I'll accept the position as Mitsuki's producer.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.050
C-Conditions?!

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:29.430
If you want something...

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.850
I don't care about money.

00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:34.220
I'll get to make music again after all.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:38.230
Then...

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:40.270
Then... what are the conditions?

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.270
If it's something that we can do...

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:44.360
My conditions are...

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:46.650
Mitsuki-chan...

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:47.320
Ah, yes...

00:19:48.110 --> 00:19:49.200
First...

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.570
...you have to get your throat checked regularly.

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:53.080
Second...

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.870
...when the time comes, promise to listen to what I said before

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:57.830
We'll do the surgery, 'kay?

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:00.170
S-Surgery?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.290
That's...

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.240
Of course, I'll be the one doing the operation.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.050
I'll have to stop working full-time...

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.760
...and work part-time instead, though.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:08.420
Eh?

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:23.880
Sensei...

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.230
I have my own reasons as well.

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:29.360
I really can't forget about music.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.950
To tell you the truth, I actually wanted to resign...

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:37.580
But there's something besides 
music that I must do, after all.

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:42.000
That is... to heal Mitsuki-chan's throat.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.210
Sensei...

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:47.670
I want to hear Mitsuki-chan sing <i>Eternal Snow </i> as well.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:51.220
Your father in heaven...

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.470
and your mother...

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:53.930
I want to let them hear it!

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:55.850
I...

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:58.140
...believe in you, Wakaouji-sensei.

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:01.640
With your help, I'll be able to shine even more than before.

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:03.560
That's what I plan to do.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:05.820
I'm going to help you shine more and more...

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.900
...until Eichi-kun notices you.

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:08.860
Okay!

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:10.900
Also...

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.410
Here.

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:15.200
You dropped it in your room at the hospital.

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.990
I asked around, but no one knew what it was.

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.370
I figured it was probably yours.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:24.040
Thank you, Wakaouji-sensei.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:25.790
I'm counting on you!

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:29.260
So am I, Mitsuki-chan.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.050
No... <i>Full Moon.</i>

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:31.760
Okay!

00:23:07.270 --> 00:23:09.310
What are you fretting over, Meroko?

00:23:09.310 --> 00:23:13.530
It's great that we asked Wakaouji-sensei to be the producer for her new song, but...

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:16.200
...he won't let her sing at all!

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:20.660
And then, he asks Mitsuki questions like "What do you want to tell people through your song?"

00:23:20.660 --> 00:23:23.200
At this rate, we'll never get it recorded.

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:23.990
It's fine.

00:23:23.990 --> 00:23:26.500
She'll definitely find an answer!

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.330
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:31.030
What I Want to Say...
